# PROJECT CHARTER 

## Project Title: Emergency Department Patient Flow Transformation


# DOCUMENT PURPOSE
The purpose of this Project Charter is to formally authorise the Emergency Department Patient Flow Transformation project and provide a clear foundation for planning, execution, governance, and delivery.
This document defines the project purpose, objectives, scope, stakeholders, responsibilities, assumptions, constraints, and success criteria.


# PROJECT BACKGROUND 
Northbridge NHS Foundation Trust is experiencing significant challenges within Emergency Department operations, including increasing patient demand, extended waiting times, limited visibility of available beds, delayed patient transfers, and inefficient communication between clinical and operational teams.
A digital transformation programme has been proposed to improve patient flow through enhanced bed management, better information visibility, improved processes, and effective project governance.


# PROJECT PURPOSE 
The purpose of this project is to design and implement a digital patient flow transformation approach that improves Emergency Department efficiency while maintaining patient safety, regulatory compliance, and quality of care.


# PROJECT AIM 

To improve Emergency Department patient flow by introducing an AI-assisted bed management solution supported by effective governance, stakeholder engagement, and change management.


# PROJECT OBJECTIVES 

The project objectives are:

## Objective 1

Reduce Emergency Department waiting times by improving patient movement and bed allocation processes.

## Objective 2

Provide real-time visibility of hospital capacity and available beds.

## Objective 3

Improve communication between Emergency Department teams, wards, and operational managers.

## Objective 4

Reduce delays caused by inefficient discharge and transfer processes.

## Objective 5

Improve decision-making through data-driven insights and predictive analytics.

## Objective 6

Ensure the solution complies with NHS information governance and cybersecurity requirements.


